 "title": "core", "category": "Framework", "author": "irpina",
 "description": "The boot copier and the hook bus for the Octatrack: it reserves the bottom of the sample and recorder memory for mods, only the 6 KB pages their RAM fills (0.2 took 10 MB), copies their code there at boot and checks the copy against the linker's hash (it halts on a mismatch rather than run it), and calls them on the UI tick, the screen, the keys, the encoders, MIDI in and out, the audio frame, its start and its end, the transport, the end of boot, the idle loop and a 120 Hz tick. It times every audio frame, writes page-2 knobs the way the panel does, and paces MIDI out. From 0.6 it tells mods when a project is loaded, made, saved and reloaded, runs their card work on the engine task, keeps their data with the project and on the card in files the stock OS ignores, and gives them battery RAM. From 0.7 it tells mods when a voice starts, releases, binds to its sample, ends and has its locks applied, and when the DSP's record and trig flags for a track are written, and lets them change or take the ones that can be. From 0.8 it tells mods of the edits their data must follow (a pattern or a track through the clipboard and the undo buffer, where a paste or an undo may be refused; a Part saved, reloaded, changed or set to its defaults; the start of a project load), of a voice about to be reset (it may be kept), of the boot before the OS, and lets them change the track icons and the SETUP windows' knobs. From 0.9 it tells mods each time a track's mute changes, and lets them choose what the Part keeps of it. From 0.10 it tells mods when a pattern's Part is applied, a pattern is added to the chain, the sequencer stops and resets, and the all-notes-off goes out. From 0.11 it lets a mod take the held-step editor's encoder turns, tells it of the pattern data's copies before they happen, and of each note a MIDI track sends. From 0.12 it lets a mod set the length each track wraps at, and tells it when the pattern wraps. From 0.13 it lets a mod set the length of a recorder's take, and from 0.14 the pattern each track plays. From 0.15 it calls mods on the UI task's tick, and from 0.16 on each card command and each task switch. From 0.17 mods can draw beside a track tab's letter; from 0.18 they hear when a card command finishes and when the battery-RAM settings are loaded; from 0.19 they can change each LFO's step, and from 0.20 take the scene-lock knob's turns; from 0.21 the TEMPO key and ARP SETUP's knobs too; from 0.22 ev_setup_dial also covers SRC / NOTE SETUP and ARP SETUP; from 0.23 mods can change what the knob widget of RECORDING SETUP draws; from 0.24 they set the panel's LEDs before each flush, and from 0.25 draw over the trig mode box; from 0.26 ev_setup_dial also covers the MIDI CTRL pages' knobs, and from 0.27 mods hear each per-bank SAVE and RELOAD copy. Every linkable Octatrack mod needs it. On its own it changes nothing else the unit does.",
 "device": "octatrack", "os": "1.40C",
 "sources": ["core-ot.s", "bus.s", "exports.c", "store.s", "store.c", "voice.s",
